Critical implementation rule

If a feature already exists and works properly, preserve it.

If it exists but has a poor user experience, improve it without destroying its existing functionality.

If it exists partially, complete it.

If it does not exist, add it.

If an existing feature already solves a problem adequately, DO NOT introduce another feature that performs the same job.

The goal is to improve the existing product, not inflate it with unnecessary functionality.

