FINAL PRODUCT STANDARD

The final Swiftvero Express website should feel like a serious international-standard logistics technology platform.

A first-time individual customer should find it easy to send a package.

An e-commerce entrepreneur should be able to manage multiple customer shipments without repetitive manual work.

An importer should understand the available freight options and the information needed for a quotation.

A corporate customer should be able to organise shipping records and manage authorised users.

A diaspora customer should be able to understand the shipment process and receive useful updates.

Every customer should understand what is happening and what to do next.

The objective is not to build the website with the most features. The objective is to build a website that solves the most important customer problems through the simplest possible experience.

Make professional design decisions independently. Do not ask me to approve every small design choice.

However, inspect the existing application before changing it, preserve all working functionality, and implement the upgrade carefully.

Begin with the full audit and feature mapping, then proceed with the implementation.

